                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure for Kan complexes
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_cisinski_model_structure"} As a Cisinski model structure
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#GeneralProperties"} General properties
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelToInfGrpds"}
                    Relation to the model structure for
                    = succeed "-groupoids" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %li
                %a{:href => "#history"} History
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            satisfying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Kan+complex"} weak Kan filler conditions
            that make it behave like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            – the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Joyal
              model structure
            or
            %strong model structure for quasi-categories
            – such that the fibrant objects are precisely the quasi-categories and the weak equivalences precisely the correct
            %em categorical equivalences
            that generalize the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #TheModelStructure.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              The
              %strong model structure for quasi-categories
              or
              %strong Joyal model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              has
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  are the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  are those maps that are taken by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigidification+of+quasi-categories"} rigidification
                  functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℭ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{C}
                  (the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  to the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+equivalence"} Dwyer-Kan equivalence
                  (a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                  in the
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan-Bergner+model+structure+on+sSet-enriched+categories"} Dwyer-Kan-Bergner model structure on sSet-enriched categories
            %p
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_a_cisinski_model_structure As a Cisinski model structure
          %p
            The model structure for quasi-categories is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski model structure
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            whose class of weak equivalences is the localizer generated by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
            inclusions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi Sp
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Sp^n \hookrightarrow \Delta^n\}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Ara"} Ara
          %h3#GeneralProperties General properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p The model structure for quasi-categories is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper model category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
          %p
          #CartesianProductPreservesWeakCategoricalEquivalences.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              The image under the
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+categorical+equivalences"} weak categorical equivalences
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheModelStructure"}
          \&amp;lbrack;
          %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie (2009), Cor. 2.2.5.4
          \&amp;rbrack;
          #CartesianMonoidalModelStructure.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The model structure for quasi-categories is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
              (hence a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+model+category"} cartesian closed model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              over itself, hence is
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Joyal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C2%29-category"} (infinity,2)-category
              %em not
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
              a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a fibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              precisely if both of the following conditions hold:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
                %p
                  in that for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                  and a lift of its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                  through
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  to an equivalence in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal"} Joyal
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie (2009), cor. 2.4.6.5
          %p
            So every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              are precisely those that are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibrant
              over the point, hence those simplicial sets which are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %p
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie (2009), theorem 2.4.6.1
            \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#RelToInfGrpds
            Relation to the model structure for
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
            has a left and a right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi grpdfy
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi i
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Core
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi grpdfy
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (grpdfy \dashv i \dashv Core)
                  \\;\;
                  \\colon
                  \\;\;
                  (\infty,1)Cat
                  \\stackrel{\overset{grpdfy}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{Core}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  \\infty Grpd
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Core
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core
                is the operation of taking the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-category;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi grpdfy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} grpdfy
                is the operation of
                %em groupoidification
                that freely generates an
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, around remark 1.2.5.4
          %p
            The adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi grpdfy
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (grpdfy \dashv i)
            is modeled by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
          #eq:BousfieldLocalizationToKanQuillenStructure.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Id
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mi Id
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sSet_{Quillen}
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{Id}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{Id}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\;\; \bot \;\;}
                  sSet_{Joyal}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %mi Id
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L} Id \colon (sSet_{Joyal})^\circ \to (sSet_{Quillen})^\circ
            takes a fibrant object on the left – a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            – then does nothing to it but regarding it now as an object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            and then producing its fibrant replacement there, which is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
            %em groupoidification
            \.
          %p The other adjunction is given by the following
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mo !
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi k
                            %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (k_! \dashv k^!)
                    \\;\; \colon
                    sSet_{Quillen}
                    \\stackrel
                    {\overset{k^!}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\underset{k_!}{\longrightarrow}}
                    sSet_{Joyal}
            %p
              which arises as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k : \Delta \to sSet : [n] \mapsto \Delta'[n]
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^'[n] = N(\{0 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} 1 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \cdots \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} n\})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              freely generated from the linear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            %p
              This means that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SSet
              we have
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi sSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^!(X)_n  = Hom_{sSet}(\Delta'[n],X)
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mo !
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi n
                          %mo =
                          %msup
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi k
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_!(X)_n = \int^{[k]} X_k \cdot \Delta'[k]
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney07"}> Joyal &amp; Tierney (2007), prop 1.19
            )
          %p
            The following proposition shows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k_! \dashv k^!)
            is indeed a model for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i \dashv Core)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For any
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi sSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sSet
                  the canonical morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to k_!(X)
                  is an acyclic cofibration in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi sSet
                            %mi Quillen
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi sSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sSet
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Core
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^!(X) \to Core(X)
                  is an acyclic fibration in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi sSet
                            %mi Quillen
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney07"}> Joyal &amp; Tierney (2007), prop 1.20
            )
          %h2#history History
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
            on the history of the Joyal model structure (also on
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/425082/when-did-the-joyal-model-structure-on-simplicial-sets-originate/427514#427514"} MathOverflow
          %blockquote
            %p I became interested in quasi-categories (without the name) around 1980 after attending a talk by Jon Beck on the work of Boardman and Vogt. I wondered if category theory could be extended to quasi-categories. In my mind, a crucial test was to show that a quasi-category is a Kan complex if its homotopy category is a groupoid. All my attempts at showing this have failed for about 15 years, until I stopped trying hard! I found a proof after extending to quasi-categories a few basic notions of category theory. This was around 1995. The model structure for quasi-categories was discovered soon after. I did not publish it immediately because I wanted to show that it could be used for proving something new in homotopy theory. I am a bit of a perfectionist (and overly ambitious?). I was hoping to develop a synthesis between category theory and homotopy theory (hence the name quasi-categories). I met Lurie at a conference organised by Carlos Simpson in Nice (in 2001?). I gave a talk on the model structure and Lurie asked for a copy of my notes afterward.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %p
            A similar model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-categories"} (∞,n)-categories
            is discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+cellular+sets"} model structure on cellular sets
          %p
            There are analogues of the Joyal model structure for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+sets"} cubical sets
            (with or without connection):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+cubical+quasicategories"} model structure for cubical quasicategories
          %h2#references References
          %p The original construction of the Joyal model structure is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"}> Andre Joyal
              ,
              %em Theory of quasi-categories I
          %p Unfortunately, this never became publicly available, but see the lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Joyal08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Theory+of+Quasi-Categories+and+its+Applications"} The Theory of Quasi-Categories and its Applications
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://lists.lehigh.edu/pipermail/algtop-l/2007q4/000017.html"} Advanced Course on Simplicial Methods in Higher Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.cat/~kock/crm/hocat/advanced-course/Quadern45-2.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p or the construction of the model structure in Cisinski’s book
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher categories and homotopical algebra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.uni-regensburg.de/cisinski/CatLR.pdf"} pdf
          %p which closely follows Joyal’s original construction.
          %p
            A proof that proceeds via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+categories"} simplicially enriched categories
          %ul
            %li#Lurie09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , following Thm. 2.2.5.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 170
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/titles/8957.html"} pup:8957
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On the relation to the model structure for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces"} complete Segal spaces
          %ul
            %li#JoyalTierney07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"}> Andre Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quasi-categories vs. Segal spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categories in Algebra, Geometry and Mathematical Physics
              %strong 431
              (2007) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0607820"}> arXiv:math/0607820
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/conm/431"} doi:10.1090/conm/431
          %p
            Discussion with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structures"} Cisinski model structures
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+cellular+sets"} model structure on cellular sets
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Ara
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dimitri+Ara"}> Dimitri Ara
              ,
              %em Higher quasi-categories vs higher Rezk spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.4354"}> arXiv
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algèbre homotopique et catégories supérieures
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/coursinftycat.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On a model structure for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C2%29-sheaves"} (infinity,2)-sheaves
            with values in quasicategories:
          %ul
            %li#Meadows15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Meadows"}> Nicholas Meadows
              ,
              %em The Local Joyal Model Structure
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1507.08723"}> arXiv:1507.08723
              )
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transfer
            of the Joyal model structure to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+simplicial+sets"} reduced simplicial sets
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+reduced+simplicial+sets#Burke21"} Burke (2021)
